<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <!--
    If you are serving your web app in a path other than the root, change the
    href value below to reflect the base path you are serving from.

    The path provided below has to start and end with a slash "/" in order for
    it to work correctly.

    For more details:
    * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/base

    This is a placeholder for base href that will be replaced by the value of
    the `--base-href` argument provided to `flutter build`.
  -->
  <base href="$FLUTTER_BASE_HREF">

  <!--
    Self-host the Firebase JS SDK. FlutterFire dynamically imports these modules
    from www.gstatic.com at runtime; on a flaky/blocking network (uni/eduroam,
    VPN, content blocker) that import can FAIL → Firebase Auth/Functions die →
    every callable fails with no server log ("works sometimes, not others").
    This import map redirects those exact gstatic URLs to copies served from our
    OWN origin (web/firebase/*.js) → no external CDN dependency at runtime.
    Degrades gracefully: browsers without import-map support, or a future SDK
    version bump, simply fall back to gstatic. Keep the version below in sync
    with firebase_core_web's bundled SDK version (currently 12.14.0).
  -->
  <script type="importmap">
  {
    "imports": {
      "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/12.14.0/firebase-app.js": "/firebase/firebase-app.js",
      "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/12.14.0/firebase-auth.js": "/firebase/firebase-auth.js",
      "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/12.14.0/firebase-functions.js": "/firebase/firebase-functions.js",
      "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/12.14.0/firebase-firestore.js": "/firebase/firebase-firestore.js",
      "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/12.14.0/firebase-storage.js": "/firebase/firebase-storage.js",
      "https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/12.14.0/firebase-messaging.js": "/firebase/firebase-messaging.js"
    }
  }
  </script>

  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta content="IE=Edge" http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible">
  <meta name="description" content="Lokka — discover local deals, follow your favourite shops, collect stamps and rewards.">
  <!-- Brand theme colour (matches manifest theme_color) for the browser/PWA chrome. -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#1FA97E">

  <!-- iOS meta tags & icons -->
  <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent">
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Lokka">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="icons/Icon-192.png">

  <!-- Favicon -->
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png"/>

  <title>Lokka — Local Deals & Loyalty</title>
  <link rel="manifest" href="manifest.json">
</head>
<body>
  <!--
    Freshness guard: unregister stale service workers and clear their caches so
    the hosted app always runs the freshly uploaded build. This kills the
    "I re-uploaded but the browser still runs old code" class of bug on custom
    hosting (jajehelp.com). Safe: no forced reload, so no reload loop.
  -->
  <script>
    (function () {
      try {
        if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
          navigator.serviceWorker.getRegistrations().then(function (regs) {
            regs.forEach(function (r) { r.unregister(); });
          }).catch(function () {});
        }
        if (window.caches && caches.keys) {
          caches.keys().then(function (keys) {
            keys.forEach(function (k) { caches.delete(k); });
          }).catch(function () {});
        }
      } catch (e) {}
    })();
  </script>
  <script src="flutter_bootstrap.js" async></script>
</body>
</html>
